: ASM_ARCH=i386_nasm_gnu :
: BLOCK_TEST :
: RUN_ASM :

:/
Reduced from log.log failures 145, 256, 259, 445, 457 and other signed divisions.
Expected: -21 / 5 == -4, exit 42.
The i386 selector emits CQO before IDIV ECX. CQO requires 64-bit mode, so NASM
rejects the program before execution. A 32-bit dividend needs CDQ instead.
/:
@[inline(never)]
function divide488(i32 value, i32 divisor) -> i32 {
    return value / divisor;
}

start() {
    if divide488(-21i32, 5i32) != -4i32; { exit 1; }
    exit 42;
}

:/ OUTPUT
@exit_code=42
/:
